{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Liability Caps"}, {"type": "position", "content": 12}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use when talking about liability caps in a software license agreement."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Learning Outcome"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.  Writes simple texts on concepts on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, technological negotiation, and requirements on negotiation processes."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob12re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go to the internet and find as much information as you can about liability caps."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take notes and make a list of the web pages used, paying attention to use only web pages written in English."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the information found to write a summary about liability caps, don\u00b4t forget to mention the main characteristics and examples of liability caps."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the text to the class."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I analyze written information liability caps."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe important facts and characteristics related to liability caps."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I show real examples of liability caps in license agreements."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Be Supposed to in Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p><strong>Be supposed to </strong>in the question form is used to ask about things that are assumed to happen.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>When you want to ask a question about something you think is intended, required, or expected to happen, you can use <strong>be supposed to</strong> in its interrogative form.</p> <p>Structure:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">(Wh-) + Verb <strong>Be</strong>+ Subject +<strong> Supposed to</strong> + <strong>Verb in base form</strong> + Complement</p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><strong><i>Are </i></strong><i>you<strong> supposed to</strong> <strong>limit</strong> the terms for the licensor?</i></p> <p><i>What <strong>are</strong> we <strong>supposed</strong> <strong>to</strong> <strong>do</strong> if we lose sensitive data? </i></p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Is the liability of a software agreement supposed to be limited?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Is the amount of the cap supposed to change?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Which things are supposed to be excluded from the cap on liability?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Understanding the concept of Heads of loss"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>In a contract, the categories of damage that a party could incur are called <strong>heads of loss</strong>.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>Heads of loss or heads of claim are categories of damage that could be committed by a person or party. The word <strong><i>head</i></strong> is used to express <strong><i>category</i></strong>. Each head of loss refers to a particular category of responsibility.</p> <p><strong><i>Loss</i></strong> refers to the equivalent of damages at common law. Measuring damages could result very complex; however, the very first thing to do is to place the injured party in the same position as if the contract had been followed appropriately.</p> <p>The following are some of the most common heads of loss listed in the book <i>Building Contract Claims</i>:</p> <ul> <li>On-site establishment costs</li> <li>Head office overheads</li> <li>Loss of profit</li> <li>Inefficient or increased use of labor and plant</li> <li>Winter working</li> <li>Plant</li> <li>Increased costs</li> <li>Financing charges and interest&nbsp;</li> </ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cap"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "term used to express limitation or restriction"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: But how is the liability cap supposed to be calculated?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob12aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stated"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "stipulated by agreement "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Many license agreements contain a liability cap which is determined depending on the amount of fees paid by the customer during a stated period."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob12aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "damage"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "injury or hurt that reduces efficacy and affects the performance"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can even limit the type of damages that could be recovered."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob12aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "variable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "possible to change "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The amount of the cap is variable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob12aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "loss"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something ruined, lost or destroyed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is mandatory to exclude some head of loss."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob12aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "afterwards"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when something happens at a subsequent time "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The fees and the capped amount could be less than the fee paid afterwards in the term of the contract."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob12aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can understand written information about liability caps in a software license agreement. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can use concepts related to liability caps."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can write a paragraph to summarize information about liability caps. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you think it is wise to know the software vendor's potential to protect the customer's interests in the case of damage or loss of data? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "In what cases do you think a software vendor's should be made accountable for the loss or damage of data?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Liabi