ta": [{"contents": [], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Activity 3"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}], "id": 4}, {"stimuli_ids": [4], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_1"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 1}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Introduction: (state relation between the article and your text)"}], "type": "question"}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_1"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 1}], "id": 1}, {"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Body (main ideas, definitions)"}], "type": "question"}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_1"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 1}], "id": 2}, {"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Conclusion: (Review the main points and a final comments about your paragraph)"}], "type": "question"}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_1"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 1}], "id": 3}], "type": "GWR", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Writing a Summary About Liability Caps"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Instructions:<br/>\n<em>\n<ul>\n<li>Read the text and answer the following questions.</li>\n\n<li>Read the article and get the main ideas from it.</li>\n\n<li>Write a paragraph to summarize information about liability caps. (150-200 words)</li>\n</ul></em>\n\n<br/>\nWhen you have typed in ALL your answers, click the <span class=\"strong\">Go to Writing Task</span> button\n<br/><br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong><p align=\"center\">Liability Caps</p></strong>\n<p align=\"justify\">Is the liability of a software agreement supposed to be limited? Well, software license agreements have provisions that limit the amount of the software's provider liability to the customer for damage or loss. This is called liability cap.  But, how is the liability cap supposed to be calculated? Many license agreements contain a liability cap which is determined depending on the amount of fees paid by the customer during a stated period. <br/></br>\n\nYou can even limit the type of damages that could be recovered. This would limit the liability and recover to only certain damages. In this sense, is the amount of the cap supposed to change? Totally. The amount of the cap is variable. So, if an event of loss happens in the first three months of the agreement, the fees and the capped amount could be less than the fee paid afterwards in the term of the contract. On the other hand, if the customer accepts a cap of liability, it's advisable to include a floor amount in the cap.<br/></br>\n \nIt means that the cap of liability is the greater of a specified amount in the next 12 months. Which things are supposed to be excluded from the cap on liability? It is mandatory to exclude some head of loss, like a breach of privacy, confidentiality, and personal injury. All in all, a financial cap either limits or expands the liability. Whatever limitation of liability and indemnification that is applied must be understood and agreed by both parties to avoid claims by the licensor. </p>\n<br/>\n\nFollow this plan to write your short text:"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Activity 3"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Time to review your text. </br></br></strong>\n<span class =\"italic\">\nDid you include the main ideas you found reading about liability caps? </br></br>\n\nWhen you are writing your text, remember to include: </br>\n<ul>\n<li>The introduction making a relation between your paragraph and the original text. </li>\n\n<li>Important aspects and main ideas about liability caps. </li>\n \n<li>A conclusion about the information you found and what you wrote in the summary. </li>\n</ul>\n</br>Proofread your text for grammar, spelling and punctuation errors. </br></br>\n\nClick the <span class =\"strong\">Submit</span> button to save your work."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"grading_contents": {"body": {"rows": [{"cells": [{"content_type": "text", "colspan": 1, "element": "th", "content": ""}, {"content_type": "text", "colspan": 1, "element": "th", "points": "20", "content": [" "]}, {"content_type": "text", "colspan": 1, "element": "th", "points": "20", "content": [" "]}, {"content_type": "text", "colspan": 1, "element": "th", "points": "20", "content": [" "]}, {"content_type": "text", "colspan": 1, "element": "th", "points": "20", "content": [" "]}]}, {